\begin{remark}
  The fact that one ancilla is always sufficient in
  Theorem~\ref{thm-main} is primarily of theoretical interest. In
  practice, one may assume that on most quantum computing
  architectures, ancillas are relatively cheap. Moreover, the use of
  additional ancillas can significantly reduce the size and depth
  of the generated circuits (see e.g.~\cite{Selinger-toffoli}).
\end{remark}

